#: src/ui/game.rs:583
msgid "Tick what you got:"
msgstr "Zaznacz, co trafiłeś:"

#: src/ui/game.rs:649
msgid "Right!"
msgstr "Dobrze!"

#: src/ui/game.rs:651
msgid "Not this time."
msgstr "Tym razem nie."

#: src/ui/game.rs:672
msgid "The cover is mostly"
msgstr "Okładka jest głównie"

#. Translators: Guessing game: points scored for this song. {points} is a number.
#: src/ui/game.rs:690
#, rust-format
msgid "+{points} points"
msgstr "+{points} pkt"

#: src/sink.rs:1577
msgid "Next song"
msgstr "Następny utwór"

#: src/demo.rs:2400
msgid "Lyrics are hidden while you guess"
msgstr "Tekst jest ukryty podczas zgadywania"

#: src/ui/lyrics.rs:134
msgid "They come back when the song is revealed."
msgstr "Wróci po odkryciu utworu."

#. Guessing game: every song of the game has been played.
#: src/ui/game.rs:389
msgid "Game over"
msgstr "Koniec gry"

#: src/ui/game.rs:395
msgid "Play again"
msgstr "Zagraj ponownie"

#. Guessing game: a song from elsewhere, or one already guessed, is playing.
#: src/ui/game.rs:403
msgid "The playing song is not one to guess."
msgstr "Odtwarzany utwór nie jest do zgadywania."

#: src/ui/game.rs:408
msgid "Continue the game"
msgstr "Kontynuuj grę"

#. Guessing game: the cover is being read for its colours.
#: src/ui/game.rs:593
msgid "Reading the cover…"
msgstr "Odczytywanie okładki…"

#. Guessing game: the cover could not be read, or too few covers were found.
#: src/ui/game.rs:707
msgid "This song could not be scored."
msgstr "Nie udało się ocenić tego utworu."

#: src/ui/queue.rs:362
msgid "The queue is hidden while the guessing game plays."
msgstr "Kolejka jest ukryta podczas gry w zgadywanie."

#. Translators: A setting: what Sirensong custom order arranges of playlists and folders also moves in the Spotify library, both ways.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:2671
msgid "Keep in step with Spotify"
msgstr "Synchronizuj ze Spotify"

#. Translators: A setting: what happens when Sirensong custom order and the Spotify library were both rearranged while apart.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:2673
msgid "When both changed"
msgstr "Gdy obie się zmieniły"

#: src/ui/settings.rs:2679
msgid "Moving a playlist or folder in Sirensong custom order moves it in your Spotify library too, and changes made in Spotify's apps come here. Albums, artists, podcasts, Liked Songs and Local Files are arranged only in Sirensong."
msgstr "Przeniesienie playlisty lub folderu we własnej kolejności Sirensong przenosi je też w bibliotece Spotify, a zmiany wprowadzone w aplikacjach Spotify trafiają tutaj. Albumy, wykonawców, podcasty, Polubione utwory i Pliki lokalne układa się tylko w Sirensong."

#: src/ui/settings.rs:2686
msgid "When Sirensong custom order and your Spotify library were both rearranged apart: show both and choose, take Spotify's, or keep this computer's and send it to Spotify."
msgstr "Gdy własna kolejność Sirensong i biblioteka Spotify zostały przestawione osobno: pokaż obie i wybierz, weź tę ze Spotify albo zachowaj tę z tego komputera i wyślij ją do Spotify."

#. Translators: When both orders changed: show both and choose each time.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:2705
msgid "Ask me"
msgstr "Pytaj"

#. Translators: When both orders changed: take the Spotify library's.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:2707
msgid "Spotify's"
msgstr "Spotify"

#. Translators: When both orders changed: keep Sirensong custom order.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:2709
msgid "Mine"
msgstr "Moja"

#. Translators: {name} is a folder name in Sirensong custom order.
#: src/ui/dialogs.rs:67
msgid "“{name}” will be removed from Sirensong custom order. What it holds stays where it is."
msgstr "„{name}” zostanie usunięty z własnej kolejności Sirensong. To, co zawiera, zostanie na swoim miejscu."

#. Translators: Sirensong custom order and the Spotify library were both rearranged while apart.
#: src/ui/dialogs.rs:98
msgid "Both orders changed"
msgstr "Obie kolejności się zmieniły"

#: src/ui/dialogs.rs:100
msgid "Sirensong custom order and your Spotify library were rearranged apart. Choose which to keep: the other follows it. What only Sirensong arranges stays either way."
msgstr "Własna kolejność Sirensong i biblioteka Spotify zostały przestawione osobno. Wybierz, którą zachować: druga się do niej dostosuje. To, co układa tylko Sirensong, zostaje w obu przypadkach."

#. Translators: Heading over what changed in the Spotify library.
#: src/ui/dialogs.rs:112
msgid "On Spotify"
msgstr "W Spotify"

#. Translators: Heading over what changed in Sirensong custom order.
#: src/ui/dialogs.rs:114
msgid "In Sirensong"
msgstr "W Sirensong"

#: src/ui/dialogs.rs:119
msgid "No changes"
msgstr "Brak zmian"

#. Translators: Keep Sirensong custom order and send it to Spotify.
#: src/ui/dialogs.rs:151
msgid "Keep mine"
msgstr "Zachowaj moją"

#. Translators: Take the Spotify library's arrangement into Sirensong custom order.
#: src/ui/dialogs.rs:155
msgid "Use Spotify's"
msgstr "Użyj ze Spotify"

#. Translators: A line of the conflict dialog. {name} is a playlist or folder, {folder} the folder it moved into.
#: src/app.rs:6872
msgid "{name} moved into {folder}"
msgstr "{name} przeniesiono do {folder}"

#. Translators: A line of the conflict dialog. {name} is a playlist or folder that moved, outside any folder.
#: src/app.rs:6878
msgid "{name} moved"
msgstr "{name} przeniesiono"

#. Translators: A line of the conflict dialog. {name} is a playlist or folder that was added.
#: src/app.rs:6882
msgid "{name} added"
msgstr "{name} dodano"

#. Translators: A line of the conflict dialog. {name} is a playlist or folder that was removed.
#: src/app.rs:6886
msgid "{name} removed"
msgstr "{name} usunięto"

#. Translators: A line of the conflict dialog. {name} is the folder's new name.
#: src/app.rs:6889
msgid "Folder renamed to {name}"
msgstr "Zmieniono nazwę folderu na {name}"

#. Translators: A setting: choosing Tree or Circles for the playlist map chooses it on Home and in the Library both.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:1349
msgid "Same map view on Home and in the Library"
msgstr "Ten sam widok mapy w Start i w Bibliotece"

#. Translators: A setting: while Home shows the playlist map, the Library shows its list or grid instead of a second map.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:1351
msgid "One map at a time"
msgstr "Jedna mapa naraz"

#. Translators: A setting: which results a new search shows first, all mixed or one kind.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:1353
msgid "Search opens on"
msgstr "Wyszukiwanie otwiera się na"

#: src/ui/settings.rs:1503
msgid "Off, Home's map and the Library's each keep their own choice of Tree or Circles."
msgstr "Wyłączone: mapa w Start i mapa w Bibliotece zachowują osobno wybór Drzewa lub Okręgów."

#: src/ui/settings.rs:1510
msgid "While Home shows the map, the Library shows its list or grid."
msgstr "Gdy Start pokazuje mapę, Biblioteka pokazuje listę lub siatkę."

#: src/ui/settings.rs:1517
msgid "The results a new search shows first: all of them, or one kind."
msgstr "Wyniki, które nowe wyszukiwanie pokazuje najpierw: wszystkie lub jeden rodzaj."

#. Translators: Player bar visualizer: the spectrum and the waveform together.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:1790
msgid "Both"
msgstr "Oba"

#. Translators: Hover text on the Library's map views while Home shows the playlist map, with one map at a time.
#: src/ui/sidebar.rs:2442
msgid "Home shows the map now"
msgstr "Start pokazuje teraz mapę"

#. Translators: A setting: while the playlist map is open, the Library's search box sits above the map.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:1355
msgid "Search box above the map"
msgstr "Pole wyszukiwania nad mapą"

#. Translators: A setting: searching marks what matches on the playlist map instead of filtering it.
#: src/ui/settings.rs:1357
msgid "Search marks matches on the map"
msgstr "Wyszukiwanie zaznacza trafienia na mapie"

#: src/ui/settings.rs:1528
msgid "While a map is open, the Library's search box sits above it."
msgstr "Gdy mapa jest otwarta, pole wyszukiwania Biblioteki jest nad nią."

#: src/ui/settings.rs:1535
msgid "Searching rings what matches and leaves the rest in place. Off, the search is a filter, as Zoom in and Only selected treat the others."
msgstr "Wyszukiwanie obrysowuje trafienia i zostawia resztę na miejscu. Wyłączone, wyszukiwanie jest filtrem, który Przybliż i Tylko wybrane traktują jak pozostałe."
